  "question": {
    "text": "Copper crystallizes in fcc with a unit cell length of $361 \\mathrm{pm}$. What is the radius of copper atom ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$108 \\mathrm{pm}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$127 \\mathrm{pm}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n157 pm\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$181 \\mathrm{pm}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For FCC,\n$\\sqrt{2} a=4 r$ (the atoms touches each other along the face- diagonal)\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& r=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} a}{4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\times 361}{4} \\\\\n& =127 \\mathrm{pm}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}